        card(2, "Challenge-Response Authentication", "A sentry yells 'Thunder!' You reply 'Flash!' You prove you know the password without shouting it out loud.", "The server issues a random challenge Nonce R. The client replies with Response = H(Password || R). The server verifies the match without the password ever traveling across the wire.", "An eavesdropper capturing the response cannot reuse it because the next challenge will be totally different."),
        card(3, "Biometrics: What You Are", "Your face or thumbprint is your username, not your secret key: you cannot change your thumbprint if it gets leaked.", "Biometrics (fingerprint, FaceID, iris) measure physical traits. They provide high convenience and non-transferability, but false acceptance rates and revocability limitations require secure hardware enclaves.", "Fingerprint templates are stored as fuzzy mathematical hashes in device Secure Elements, never sent to cloud servers.")
